<section class="block-section story">
  <span class="section-tag">Story</span>
  <h2>What today is about</h2>
  <p class="sub">Two questions run this course: one for the whole year, one for this unit.</p>
  <p>The year's question is <em>How do you live well on a changing Earth?</em> Every unit comes back to it. This unit's question is <em>How do scientists know what they know, and how should we know what we know?</em> For the next seven blocks, that is the one doing the work.</p>
  <p>The anchor skill for the whole year is <strong>OPVL</strong>: Origin, Purpose, Value, Limitations. It's the framework you'll apply to every paper, news article, government report, and AI output we touch this year. We learn it here first, and we come back to it in every later unit at increasing difficulty.</p>
  <p>Everything in this class is a routine you'll meet again. The full list lives at <a href="/foundations/how-this-class-works/">How This Class Works</a>.</p>
</section>

